---
// The sponsor page. Hidde, 2026-08-26: "ik zou wel 'sponsor this project'
// gewoon live zetten, zodat we hopelijk in ieder geval de kosten kunnen
// dekken", and with it "zodat apple niet mee profiteert", which is why the
// ask lives on the web where no store takes a cut.
//
// A utility page like /privacy, /terms and /app rather than a blueprint
// contract: it targets no query and enters no internal-link scheme, so hard
// rule 7 is not in play. It carries no price of its own for the same reason
// the app cannot: the amounts live in Hidde's own provider dashboard, which
// keeps pricing where hard rule 2 puts it.
//
// SPONSOR_URL empty means: no button, noindex, and no footer link. Nothing
// here promises that anything stays free, because that promise is his to
// make and he has ruled against making it.
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Breadcrumbs from "../components/Breadcrumbs.astro";
import { breadcrumbSchema, ldScript, SITE_SCHEMA, BASE_URL } from "../lib/schema";
import { SPONSOR_URL } from "../lib/site-config";
import { submitLink } from "../lib/tree-copy";
import { pressNumbers, nf } from "../lib/press";
import { imgSrcset, creditRequired, creditName } from "../lib/images";
import { getCollection } from "astro:content";

const n = pressNumbers();

// One photograph, and it is the oldest tree on the map that has one. A page
// asking somebody to keep this going should show what it is for, and every
// comparable page does exactly that: OpenStreetMap runs six photographs of
// its map in real use. Ours is picked from the data rather than pinned by
// hand, so it cannot rot when that tree's photo changes.
const cities = await getCollection("cities");
let hero: { url: string; license?: string | null; attribution?: string | null;
            name: string; city: string; age: string } | null = null;
let oldest = -1;
for (const c of cities) {
  for (const t of (c.data.trees ?? [])) {
    const p: any = t.photo ?? {};
    const min = Number(t.age_min ?? 0);
    if (p.status === "approved" && p.url && min > oldest) {
      oldest = min;
      hero = { url: p.url, license: p.license, attribution: p.attribution,
               name: t.name, city: c.data.city, age: t.age_estimate ?? "" };
    }
  }
}
const live = SPONSOR_URL.length > 0;
const canonical = `${BASE_URL}/sponsor`;
const crumbItems: [string, string | null][] = [["Home", BASE_URL], ["Sponsor", null]];

const description = `Ancient Trees is free to use and not free to make. Sponsoring pays the bill behind ${n.cities} cities and puts the next one on the map.`;

const graph = [
  ...SITE_SCHEMA,
  breadcrumbSchema(crumbItems, canonical),
  {
    "@type": "WebPage",
    name: "Sponsor Ancient Trees",
    description,
    url: canonical,
  },
];

const headExtra = (live ? "" : '<meta name="robots" content="noindex">') + ldScript(graph);
---
<Base title="Sponsor Ancient Trees" description={description} canonical={canonical} headExtra={headExtra}>
<main class="content-page sponsor-page">
  <Breadcrumbs items={crumbItems} />
  <h1>Sponsor this project</h1>
  <p class="lede">Ancient Trees is free to use. It is not free to make.</p>

  {hero && (
    <figure class="sponsor-hero">
      <img {...imgSrcset(hero.url, [700, 1100, 1600], "(max-width: 800px) 100vw, 760px")}
           alt={`${hero.name} in ${hero.city}`} loading="eager" />
      <figcaption>
        {hero.name}, {hero.city}{hero.age ? `, ${hero.age}` : ""}.
        {creditRequired(hero.license) && creditName(hero.attribution)
          ? ` Photo: ${creditName(hero.attribution)} (${hero.license})`
          : ""}
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  )}

  <div class="prose-block">
    <p>This is one of {nf(n.trees)} trees on the map, in {n.cities} cities. Each one was found, checked against at least two independent sources, placed on the map by hand and written up, because a tree nobody can find and nobody can trust is not worth the walk. That is days of work per city, and the map behind it arrives as a bill every month whether anybody visits or not.</p>

    {live && (
      <p>
        <a class="go-btn" href={SPONSOR_URL} rel="noopener" data-ev="sponsor-open">Sponsor Ancient Trees</a>
      </p>
    )}

    <h2>What your money does</h2>
    <p>It puts the next city on the map. That is the honest unit: not a feature, not a server upgrade, a city that did not exist here last week and its trees that nobody had written down in one place. What is left over pays the monthly bill behind the {n.cities} already on it.</p>

    <h2>What you get for it</h2>
    <p>Nothing extra, and that is deliberate. Sponsoring is not a subscription and it unlocks no feature. It pays for the trees that are not on the map yet.</p>

    <h2>Helping without money</h2>
    <p>Worth just as much, and some days worth more: <a href={submitLink("tree")}>send us a tree we are missing</a>, or tell us when something on a page is wrong. People who have stood in front of the tree are how this map gets better, and a wrong pin gets looked at the same day.</p>

    {live ? (
      <p>
        <a class="go-btn" href={SPONSOR_URL} rel="noopener" data-ev="sponsor-open-foot">Sponsor Ancient Trees</a>
      </p>
    ) : (
      <p class="suggest">The sponsor page is being set up. In the meantime, <a href={submitLink("tree")}>a tree we are missing</a> helps just as much.</p>
    )}

    <h2>Who is behind it</h2>
    <p>One person in the Netherlands, working on this most days, with the research and the map built out in the open. The project has never taken money from anyone, which is why the bill is worth mentioning at all. Questions about any of it: <a href={submitLink("correction")}>send a message</a>.</p>
  </div>
</main>
</Base>
